{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/883410-spirits-and-vampires","id":883410,"title":"Spirits and vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-05T19:41:12-07:00","id":883410,"title":"Spirits and vampires","content":"A few thoughts. I recently read <i>freak legion</i> and it had some interesting things to say about how banes trying to possess vampires really just got themselves trapped for a very long lifetime, Like An unnoticeable diablorie with no effect. That, with some other information on Dark thaumaturgy, I thought of some scenarios. <br /> <br /> - If you diablorise someone, and a demon has a claim on your victim's soul, do demons come for you since you now posses their soul? <br /> <br /> - A box in the corner of the Dark thaumaturgy section of Rites of the Blood suggested that the demons described could be Fallen, Rare forms of spectres or corrupt spirits? I would assume fallen for teaching one power, but could the others teach one dark thaumaturgy? I mean spirits give out gifts, Paths aren't a huge step away from that. I don't know much about spectres, and I'd suspect they don't teach powers or possess the capability or longevity to track down who personally owes them souls, but I'd quite like to tempt a Giovanni player of mine and it seems like a likely angle... <br /> <br /> - If you embrace a formori, are they cured? (Like I get that the vampires in the line to know about formori probably wouldn't, but that's a different question)<br /> <br /> - If you ghoul a formori, are they better off? Like would that alleviate some of the symptoms (most especially degeneration and impending organ failure) since it stops one from ageing, and Caine's blood has an effect on Banes. <br /> <br /> - Can one with the virtreous path diablorise a ghost? (or, well, would ghosts fall the same way banes would?) <br /> <br /> -Could one learn powers that would allow the channeling of spirits that have fallen inside a cainite? IE use the charms of things which fell inside of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T19:49:28-07:00","id":883416,"title":"","content":"1) No, because you don't &quot;possess&quot; their soul, you <i>ate</i> their soul. That soul is destroyed.<br /> <br /> 2) Not really designed for crossover, so it's entirely up to the Storyteller.<br /> <br /> 3) Probably not, no. The damage done to their bodies has already happened.<br /> <br /> 4) It would probably freeze the negative physical effects, yes.<br /> <br /> 5) No, because ghosts (and other things) are not affected by the Curse of Caine. Only vampires can be Diablerized, since that involves devouring their cursed blood and eating their soul. Both steps required.<br /> <br /> 6) If there's a spirit trapped inside a Cainite (for some weird reason), then.. yeah, probably the ST could allow that vampire to invent a Path or Discipline or Ritual that gives them access to those powers. That's entirely up to the ST, of course, as most crossover rules are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T20:19:20-07:00","id":883428,"title":"","content":"There's an Innoccu power that allows you to remove the souls someone has diablorised. They're quite happy you got them out of there, so I don't think they're destroyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T02:02:07-07:00","id":883597,"title":"","content":"Wait. What? Seriously? Which book is that in? And who thought that was a good idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:42:32-07:00","id":883854,"title":"","content":"Fathers freedom, page 101 of <i>Rites of the Blood</i>. Ritual that lets you take those eaten out of their eater.<br /> <br /> Also, Telgar, It says in freak legion that most banes who try to possess vampires get trapped. They find their efforts at possession so utterly failed that the cursed blood of caine locks them in and they're powerless to escape or do anything. I think it gives an interesting ecological niche for Cainites. Like maybe they really had a trully good purpose for the world before thousands of years of selfish evil hid it. Also It means that a garou killing a leech might have something worse to kill tomorrow. But from a Leech point of view that's an untapped source of power they don't know about. The Thaumaturgical path of spirit can make fetishes, maybe one can get a hold of their own prisoners for use...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:04:42-07:00","id":883907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/883410-spirits-and-vampires?p=883597#post883597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. What? Seriously? Which book is that in? And who thought that was a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm with you. This Ritual is a terrible idea and conflicts with everything else written about Diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:03:58-07:00","id":883952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/883410-spirits-and-vampires?p=883907#post883907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm with you. This Ritual is a terrible idea and conflicts with everything else written about Diablerie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.... Maybe. After all, that's what those black lines ARE, the undigested bits of the diablerized soul. Many times there are stated to be some unquantified issues with post-diablerie &quot;indigestion&quot; where the diablerists gets minor quirks, flashes of memory, etc. from the unlife/life of his victim. So &quot;completely destroyed&quot;, no. &quot;Recoverable&quot; into ANYTHING like the original soul, probably not. It would be like rooting through excrement and trying to reassemble a meal from the &quot;undigested bits of potato&quot; and the like. I guess you could try and fill in the &quot;blanks&quot; Jurassic Park style with some kind of ectomplasmic goo/glue. But it wouldn't really end up being the same person.<br /> <br /> And, well, Inconnu can do impossible things right? It's a crap Ritual because it allows both salvation of the soul and absorption of the blood's power. Which seems like it should result in a dead vampire but, without the juicy goodness of the soul, it should be like drinking the blood of a Risen or a Mummy. It should probably not even give BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:07:46-07:00","id":883960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/883410-spirits-and-vampires?p=883416#post883416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) 5) No, because ghosts (and other things) are not affected by the Curse of Caine. Only vampires can be Diablerized, since that involves devouring their cursed blood and eating their soul. Both steps required.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all you did to the &quot;soul&quot; of the wraith was put them into a Destruction Harrowing, by reducing their Corpus to 0. If the wraith survives (entirely possible), s/he'll pop back up at her most powerful Fetter. If not, then it is Oblivion that gets the wraith's soul, not the vampire. <br /> <br /> Plus, as you said, it's the &quot;two great tastes that taste great together&quot;. Not only is there no soul to suck (slippery little buggers when there's nothing to anchor them), there's no actual cursed blood either. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:22:55-07:00","id":883971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/883410-spirits-and-vampires?p=883952#post883952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well.... Maybe. After all, that's what those black lines ARE, the undigested bits of the diablerized soul. Many times there are stated to be some unquantified issues with post-diablerie &quot;indigestion&quot; where the diablerists gets minor quirks, flashes of memory, etc. from the unlife/life of his victim. So &quot;completely destroyed&quot;, no. &quot;Recoverable&quot; into ANYTHING like the original soul, probably not. It would be like rooting through excrement and trying to reassemble a meal from the &quot;undigested bits of potato&quot; and the like. I guess you could try and fill in the &quot;blanks&quot; Jurassic Park style with some kind of ectomplasmic goo/glue. But it wouldn't really end up being the same person.<br /> <br /> And, well, Inconnu can do impossible things right? It's a crap Ritual because it allows both salvation of the soul and absorption of the blood's power. Which seems like it should result in a dead vampire but, without the juicy goodness of the soul, it should be like drinking the blood of a Risen or a Mummy. It should probably not even give BP.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... what happens if the Inconnu do that to Tremere or Uncle Auggie? What does it mean for the whole faith of Assamites? The implications for this are staggering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:00:24-07:00","id":884004,"title":"","content":"Well, you can all rest easier if we assume that the people you've eaten aren't inside you, consciously aware of what you are doing, and forced to live for thousands of years trapped inside you and whoever eats you too. But at least you can then keep them company..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T14:28:07-07:00","id":884907,"title":"","content":"mostly speculation but, It's been hinted that the <i>soul</i> is not the <i>vampire, </i>and it's possible the Antes let themselves be diablerized to be separated from their souls, and there's the theory that the <i>beast </i>is the <i>soul, </i>and so on...<br /> <br /> Problem is, if the <i>vampire</i> is not the <i>soul, </i>then what is it?<br /> <br /> Either way, if you consider one of these theories to be true (or half-true), you can assume that <b>whatever the <i>vampire</i> is</b> to be recoverable, but his soul remains shattered. Possibly with fragments of the diablerist's soul influencing his will, without him realizing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}